{"seq":4,"investigation_id":"inv-071ae01fa81e","recorded_at_utc":"2026-11-04T00:25:18.998842Z","type":"plan_proposed","plan":{"schema_version":"1.0","plan_id":"pln-ac1b92efc486","investigation_id":"inv-071ae01fa81e","question":"Do the podocytes this atlas calls 'endocytic' really carry LRP2 and CUBN, or is that segmentation?","dataset_id":"GSE286184","summary":"Audit LRP2 and CUBN separately in NPHS1-anchored podocytes across all 21 distinct sections (duplicate GSM8720419 excluded) under default, nucleus-only, and 1-um/2-um distance-cap assignment; persistence under strict conditions supports real carriage, while loss concentrated in distant/non-nuclear molecules supports segmentation spillover. The atlas's exact 'endocytic' podocyte subset cannot be audited because no deposited labels or frozen rule defines that subtype, and no cell-boundary polygons or morphology images are available, so this plan tests the accessible NPHS1-anchored podocyte population.","contrast":null,"cell_types":["Podocyte"],"conditions":["default","nucleus_only","distance_cap_1um","distance_cap_2um"],"steps":[{"step_id":"step-1","tool":"audit_population","arguments":{"cell_type":"Podocyte","conditions":["default","nucleus_only","distance_cap_1um","distance_cap_2um"],"genes":["LRP2"],"label_rule_id":"nphs1-anchored-v1","measure":"share_expressing","section_ids":["GSM8720409","GSM8720410","GSM8720411","GSM8720412","GSM8720413","GSM8720414","GSM8720415","GSM8720416","GSM8720417","GSM8720418","GSM8720420","GSM8720421","GSM8720422","GSM8720423","GSM8720424","GSM8720425","GSM8720426","GSM8720427","GSM8720428","GSM8720429","GSM8720430"]},"rationale":"Testing LRP2 in podocytes identified independently of LRP2/CUBN under progressively stricter molecule assignment distinguishes genuine intracellular signal from segmentation spillover."},{"step_id":"step-2","tool":"audit_population","arguments":{"cell_type":"Podocyte","conditions":["default","nucleus_only","distance_cap_1um","distance_cap_2um"],"genes":